text/plain — the DEFAULT type, and the fallback.

Recognition can never fail here: whatever nothing else claimed is text.
That is the Unix answer, and it is why a binary opens as bytes rather
than as an error — though not as an editable one: content that is not
valid UTF-8 renders with escapes and opens read-only, because the danger
was never display but round-tripping.

Roles: look, edit, properties. No shell (a store is not a channel) and
no manage (it does not run) — though text/x-python inherits these and
ADDS manage, because a Python file is text and runnable.
